return {
["19:00"]={"It was \003seven o’clock\004 when we got into the coupé with him and started for Long Island. […] So we drove on toward death through the cooling twilight.","The Great Gatsby","F. Scott Fitzgerald"},
["19:01"]={"The gates of the cemetary were closed at sundown; sundown took place that night at \003one minute past seven\004, and the distance into town is considerable.","The Filigree Ball","Anna Katherine Green"},
["19:02"]={"Twas \003about seven o’clock\004 at night,\nAnd the wind it blew with all its might,\nAnd the rain came pouring down,\nAnd the dark clouds seem’d to frown,","The Tay Bridge Disaster","William McGonagall"},
["19:03"]={"There was trouble with the track. No one could give any idea when it would be put right. The train arriving at \003three minutes past seven\004 had been the last one in. Were all the gods of travel conspiring to thwart him?","The Murder Room","P.D. James"},
["19:04"]={"Sunday evening at almost the same hour (to be precise, at about \0037:04 p.m.\004) she rings the front door bell at the home of Walter Moeding, Crime Commissioner, who is at that moment engaged, for professional rather than private reasons, in disguising himself as a sheikh.","The Lost Honour of Katharina Blum","Heinrich Böll"},
["19:05"]={"It was \003five past seven\004, a little past his normal time, when Hubert got back to the flat which he supposed he ought now to call home, but in which he still felt as ill at ease as a guest who is beginning to suspect that he has outstayed his welcome.","A Certain Justice","P.D. James"},
["19:06"]={"The time on the clock was six minutes after seven p.m. That doesn’t conclusively prove that Sam Dillon was murdered at \003seven-oh-six p.m.\004, but all other evidence would certainly corroborate that point.","In the Company of Liars","David Ellis"},
["19:07"]={"She fell into unconsciousness and so remained two days and five hours, until Tuesday evening at \003seven minutes past seven\004, when the release came. She was twenty-four years and five months old.","Chapters From My Autobiography","Mark Twain"},
["19:08"]={"It was \003eight minutes past seven\004 and still no girl. I waited impatiently. I watched another crowd surge through the barriers and move quickly down the steps. My eyes were alert for the faintest recognition.","The Girl from East Berlin","James Furner"},
["19:09"]={"Wallander was lucky and managed to catch a taxi right outside. When he got to Rosengard it was \003nine minutes past seven\004. He hoped that Mona was running late. But when he read the note on the door he realised that this was not the case.","The Pyramid","Henning Mankell"},
["19:10"]={"A taxi drew up outside her former marital home at \0037:10 p.m.\004 Alex appeared a few moments later. He was wearing a dinner jacket boasting three campaign medals.","Be Careful What You Wish For","Jeffrey Archer"},
["19:12"]={"At \003twelve minutes past seven\004, in the kitchen, Kimberly was becoming anxious.","The Private Patient","P.D. James"},
["19:13"]={"The train arrived at Kizil Arvat, two hundred and forty-two versts from the Caspian, at \003thirteen minutes past seven\004 in the evening instead of seven o’clock. The slight delay provoked thirteen objurgations from the baron, one for each minute.","The Adventures of a Special Correspondent","Jules Verne"},
["19:14"]={"If he’d lived in New York and worked in an office, he might have thrived as the typical, over-martini’d, cheating husband, leaving every night on the \0037:14\004 to White Plains, a smudge of lipstick high on his neck, and a tide of lies to see him through to the next day.","The Life and Opinions of Maf the Dog, and of his friend Marilyn Monroe","Andrew O’Hagan"},
["19:15"]={"“Your holiness,” he called.\n“Well?”\n“The horses are here; it’s time for the evening service.”\n“What o’clock is it?”\n“A \003quarter past seven\004.”","The Bishop","Anton Pavlovich Chekhov"},
["19:16"]={"“\003Sixteen past seven PM\004? That’s when he came into the store or when he left after the fact?”","The Last Precinct","Patricia Cornwell"},
["19:17"]={"Colonel Putnis knocked on his door at \0037:17 p.m.\004 The car was waiting in front of the hotel, and they drove through the dark streets to police headquarters. It had grown much colder during the evening, and the city was almost deserted.","The Dogs of Riga","Henning Mankell"},
["19:18"]={"It’s now exactly \003eighteen minutes past seven\004, according to Mr. Cartier.\nIt was still raining outside; but a taxi drove up and a couple got out and the doorman protected Gretchen with a big umbrella as she ran for the cab.","Rich Man, Poor Man","Irwin Shaw"},
["19:20"]={"The pause, we finally concluded, was to allow the other important people to catch up, those who had arrived at 7:10 waiting for those who had arrived at \0037:20\004.","Parkinson’s Law or the Pursuit of Progress","C. Northcote Parkinson"},
["19:21"]={"Gripping her gym bag in her right hand, Aomame, like Buzzcut, was waiting for something to happen. The clock display changed to \0037:21\004, then 7:22, then 7:23.","1Q84","Haruki Murakami"},
["19:22"]={"Gripping her gym bag in her right hand, Aomame, like Buzzcut, was waiting for something to happen. The clock display changed to 7:21, then \0037:22\004, then 7:23.","1Q84","Haruki Murakami"},
["19:23"]={"Gripping her gym bag in her right hand, Aomame, like Buzzcut, was waiting for something to happen. The clock display changed to 7:21, then 7:22, then \0037:23\004.","1Q84","Haruki Murakami"},
["19:24"]={"He picked up his hat and coat and Clarice said hello to him and he said hello and looked at the clock and it was \003almost twenty-five after seven\004.","The Evening’s at Seven","James Thurber"},
["19:25"]={"He picked up his hat and coat and Clarice said hello to him and he said hello and looked at the clock and it was almost \003twenty-five after seven\004.","The Evening’s at Seven","James Thurber"},
["19:26"]={"Newman pointed up at the hotel. Under the eaves shards of ice a foot long projected downwards. A palisade of icicles. Inverted. The station was little more than a one-storey hut, an isolated building with no one about. The dashboard clock registered \00319:26 hours\004.","Terminal","Colin Forbes"},
["19:27"]={"The pilot welcomed them aboard and warned them there might be a slight delay. Dexter checked his watch: \0037:27\004. He began drumming his fingers on the armrest that divided him from Scott.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["19:28"]={"It says here that you called your mother at \0037:28\004 p.m. this evening.\n“There’s some sort of mistake. I didn’t get the chance to call anyone.”","Superior Justice","Tom Hilpert"},
["19:29"]={"I expect she didn’t want Octavia to know that she’d called in her father, not until they’d worked out a plan. And I was the one who fixed the time. I didn’t see how I could catch a train before the seventeen-twenty-two which gets in to Waterloo at \003nineteen-twenty-nine\004.","A Certain Justice","P.D. James"},
["19:30"]={"When the news was over, Anderson told Gardener she was going to bed.\n“At \003seven-thirty\004?”\n“I’m still bushed.” And she looked it.","The Tommyknockers","Stephen King"},
["19:32"]={"It’s \0037:32 p.m.\004, and Marge sits beside Clay on one side of the interrogation room table. Luke and I sit opposite them. We’ve run through the preambles. The interview is being recorded.","Beneath Devil’s Bridge","Loreth Anne White"},
["19:33"]={"At \003thirty-three minutes past seven\004 he stood on the platform of the station at Southampton — a clear hour before the train containing Owen could possibly arrive. Making a few inquiries here, but too impatient to pursue his investigation carefully and inductively, he went into the town.","Desperate Remedies","Thomas Hardy"},
["19:34"]={"“You better not wait up, because if I fail, Simon, I’ll probably jump on top of you.”\n“Thanks for the warning, Mark. Tough it out, man.”\nBeautiful evening, climb into car, check watch: \0037:34\004.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["19:35"]={"George checked his watch: \0037:35 P.M.\004 By now Geoffrey Young would be taking the rest of the team through tomorrow’s program, having informed them who would be joining him on the final ascent. The water boiled.","Paths of Glory","Jeffrey Archer"},
["19:36"]={"The time on the video recorder was \00319:36\004 when the back door slammed and Victor strode into the front room clutching a handful of something so unspeakably vile it defies description.","One Foot in the Grave","David Renwick"},
["19:37"]={"A ship is making an unauthorized departure from the main orbital terminal tonight at precisely \00319:37\004 hours. We need to produce a reaction from Orbital Defense which will appear to be a genuine response to an unauthorized seizure of a vessel.","Relic of Empire","W. Michael Gear"},
["19:39"]={"At \0037:39\004 the aircraft taxied onto the runway to prepare for takeoff. When it stopped, Dexter asked the flight attendant what was holding them up.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["19:40"]={"They reckon the time was \003twenty to eight\004. They can swear, sir, that the body wasn’t suspended then and that they saw no one on the forecourt.","Original Sin","P.D. James"},
["19:41"]={"LIGHTING-UP TIME WAS \0037:41 P.M.\004 on September 25th. Krantz didn’t appear on the outskirts of Wentworth until just after eight.","False Impression","Jeffrey Archer"},
["19:42"]={"So he really had no choice but to pay an occasional visit to the living room instead, where the hands on the grandfather clock now indicated, rather unambiguously, that it was \0037:42\004","The Lincoln Highway","Amor Towles"},
["19:43"]={"In response to a hail from within the wall, several of the warders bent to the windlass, whereupon the portcullis scraped and groaned aloft, and the tall knight came riding out just as the hands of Mallory’s timepiece registered \0037:43 p.m.\004","A Knyght Ther Was","Robert F. Young"},
["19:45"]={"I imagine so. He died at night, or he was last seen alive by Grace Willson at \0037:45 p.m.\004 when he heard her confession. I suppose he died of boredom.","The Black Tower","P.D. James"},
["19:46"]={"\0037:46 P.M.\004\n“Right.” Alfred Konwitz snapped to attention. “Yes, sir.”\nHe slammed down the phone and whirled around to Jack Mulhoney. “Full denial, sir. Israeli Control says they have no military aircraft operating anywhere in that sector of the Aegean.”","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["19:47"]={"\0037:47 P.M.\004\nVance watched as the frigate got off a warning tracer, but to no effect. The Hind ignored it, as a stream of 57mm rockets from under the chopper’s stubby starboard wing flared down, while the radar-slaved machine gun beneath the nose opened fire.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["19:48"]={"\0037:48 P.M.\004\nThere are sounds of doors opening and closing, with whispered words that are like alien hisses. She senses she is in motion, on a bed that is gliding past powerful overhead lights.","Syndrome","Thomas Hoover"},
["19:49"]={"\003Eleven minutes to eight\004.\n“You’re always right; there must be a clock in your head.”\n“I can’t be wrong, tonight. I’ll be able to tell you one second before they blast off. Look! The ten-minute warning!”","The End of the Beginning","Ray Bradbury"},
["19:50"]={"The hands of the clock in the middle of the wall were pointing to \003ten minutes to eight\004. The cafe closed at eight.","Before the Coffee Gets Cold: Tales from the Cafe","Toshikazu Kawaguchi"},
["19:51"]={"The plane swung around onto the take-off runway at \0037:51\004, its jets revving before it moved slowly forward, then gathered speed. The wheels left the ground at 7:53.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["19:53"]={"The plane swung around onto the take-off runway at 7:51, its jets revving before it moved slowly forward, then gathered speed. The wheels left the ground at \0037:53\004.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["19:54"]={"The body was found at \003six minutes to eight\004. Doctor Young arrived some thirty minutes later. Just let me get that clear — I’ve a filthy memory.","A Man Lay Dead","Ngaio Marsh"},
["19:55"]={"Flora drew her coat round her, and looked up into the darkening vault of the sky. Then she glanced at her watch. It was \003five to eight\004.","Cold Comfort Farm","Stella Gibbons"},
["19:58"]={"Robert Langdon stole an anxious glance at his wristwatch: \0037:58 pm\004. The smiling face of Mickey Mouse did little to cheer him up.","The Lost Symbol","Dan Brown"},
["19:59"]={"Quickly, quickly. \003A minute to eight\004. My hot water bottle was ready, and I filled a glass with water from the tap. Time was of the essence.","The Thirteenth Tale","Diane Setterfield"},
